//ERR 13 4 13 7
//MSG="Maximum possible depth for this break statement is 0."

// There is no loop to leave, so the `brk` cannot mean anything. The message
// names the deepest level that would have been legal here — zero — rather than
// saying "not in a loop", so this and a level that merely overshoots read the
// same way; 61e_break_level_deeper_than_the_loops.cpl is the same diagnostic
// with a 1 in it.
//
// The span is the keyword alone: with no level written there is no other token
// for the statement to cover.

fn main
    brk
